            "Où est-ce que tu vas"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pron-u01-l2",
      "kind": "pron",
      "title": "u, i and ou",
      "goal": "Tell u from i, and lui from Louis.",
      "tip": {
        "title": "Same tongue as i — only the lips change",
        "body": "French i (as in \"lit\") and u (as in \"lu\") use exactly the same tongue position: only the lips differ — spread for i, tightly rounded for u. Practise \"i-u-i-u\" without moving your tongue. The combination ui (nuit, lui, suis) is a quick u gliding into i, different from the w-sound of oui and Louis."
      },
      "phrases": [
        {
          "t": "Bonne nuit !",
          "n": "Good night!"
        },
        {
          "t": "Je suis ici.",
          "n": "I'm here."
        },
        {
          "t": "Une minute !",
          "n": "Just a minute!"
        },
        {
          "t": "C'est super !",
          "n": "It's great!"
        }
      ],
